  },
  "regionNordicsLengthNote": "One to two pages. Concision is read as a virtue here.",
  "@regionNordicsLengthNote": {
    "description": "Region picker: how long a CV should run in the NORDICS market."
  },
  "regionNordicsToneNote": "Factual and team-framed. Say what the team achieved and what your part in it was; \"I single-handedly\" reads badly across the Nordics.",
  "@regionNordicsToneNote": {
    "description": "Region picker: how achievements should be framed in the NORDICS market."
  },
  "regionUkConvention1": "Two pages is the norm. One page for a recent graduate; three only for academic or very senior roles.",
  "@regionUkConvention1": {
    "description": "Region picker: one of the UK market's CV conventions, rendered as a bullet and read on its own. A complete sentence."
  },
  "regionUkConvention2": "No photograph, date of birth, marital status, or nationality. UK equality law makes them a liability for the employer as much as for you.",
  "@regionUkConvention2": {
    "description": "Region picker: one of the UK market's CV conventions, rendered as a bullet and read on its own. A complete sentence."
  },
  "regionUkConvention3": "If writing in English, use British spelling throughout: organised, programme, centre, analyse.",
  "@regionUkConvention3": {
    "description": "Region picker: one of the UK market's CV conventions, rendered as a bullet and read on its own. A complete sentence."
  },
  "regionUkConvention4": "\"References available on request\" at the foot is still expected. Do not list referees' contact details.",
